  "question": {
    "text": "A small particle of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and its retaining cord is spinning with angular velocity <math><mi>ω</mi></math> on the horizontal surface of a smooth disc. As force&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> is slightly relaxed,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> increases and <math><mi>ω</mi></math> changes. Determine the rate of change of <math><mi>ω</mi></math> with respect to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math><br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/WhatsApp_Image_2020-07-11_at_1.27.26_PM.jpeg\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 215px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
